silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_05_sections_01_concrete_anchor_2#bodymasscorrected4_0kg silm:hasLongDescription "The BodyMassCorrected4_0kg is the calibrated 4.0 kg reading from stage n+1. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Value^corrected_{n+1}', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
